  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Reconstructed constant-int64 range increment proofs after checked-private graph cloning, then bound every raw range update to a complete graph/root snapshot. Ordinary non-private functions retain the existing local proof path; private variants require graph authority, and capability-disabled, malformed, or subsequently mutated graphs retain checked arithmetic. Hostile tests alter the range stop, continue step, and root guard and verify that raw emission is revoked. On the frozen Stage-G splitting-degree catalog, all 7,081 active outputs and 9 malformed controls remain exact, static checks fall from 222 to 206, and the generated C shrinks by 1,433 bytes. A pinned 15-pair x1000 measurement improves the catalog mean from 2.085840 ms to 2.080849 ms (0.239%). The focused 38-test proof suite, strict baselib, architecture classification, a complete self-hosted build, the 326-second native correctness/performance runner, and the exact 878-second native preparation/build/test gate pass on ef93aa420. Initial native attempts are retained as receipts: they progressively exposed stale cross-worktree FLINT, FFLAS, M4RI, dist, and production-cache artifacts; after rebuilding/restoring lane-local artifacts, the unchanged gate passed.",
    "risks": [
      "The performance gain is small and measured on one pinned Linux x64 host; required non-Linux targets still rely on integration CI.",
      "The generated ELF text grows by 1,344 bytes despite fewer checks, consistent with additional specialization or inlining; keep code-size and whole-catalog timing gates when integrating.",
      "This closes a compiler proof-loss defect in the splitting-degree kernel, but does not complete the later class-group unit-reconstruction and final-result stages."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integrate this proof reconstruction with the preceding fixed-width private-graph compiler series and rerun the frozen catalog on the consolidated branch.",
      "Stop spending campaigns on sub-percent splitting-degree cleanup unless a fresh profile identifies a material regression; shift the compiler machinery into the unfinished end-to-end class-group/unit stages.",
      "Preserve the 1.39 ms mechanical C translation as a ceiling experiment and the approximately 2.08 ms integrated kernel as the compiler regression gate."
    ]
  }
